These three statements modify data. `INSERT` adds a new row; `UPDATE … SET … WHERE` changes columns in the rows that match; `DELETE FROM … WHERE` removes matching rows. The `WHERE` clause is what limits which rows are touched:
```sql
INSERT INTO products (id, name, category, price)
VALUES (5, 'Eraser', 'stationery', 0.80);

UPDATE products SET price = 2.00 WHERE id = 2;

DELETE FROM orders WHERE id = 5;
```
